{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unlikely-zealous-skua","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Amend/supersede docs/concurrency.md §I1 'permanent retention' (epic b306). Define: the horizon config key (default 30d, portable); the remote-reachability computation (a compaction commit reachable from the sync remote's tickets ref for >= N days); the stale-clone detection + FORCED remote-override protocol on reconnect (a clone whose last convergence is older than N days overrides local with remote instead of reintroducing pre-compaction events by rebase); and a proof that I1-I9 hold under it. State the accepted residual: a >N-day-drifted clone's divergent local work is discarded. Blocks S1-S3.","id":"866f-440c-3686-42df","parent_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"ADR: remote-anchored retired-event GC + stale-clone override (N-day horizon)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787594744724752001,"uuid":"063da436-6e20-4bdc-a972-fc1e80b364a2"}